<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-field-index-base="/field-index/"><head><meta charset="utf-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" /><meta name="color-scheme" content="light" /><meta name="theme-color" content="#f4f0e7" /><meta name="description" content="Coreweaver Field Index editorial policy, corrections process, and public-source standards." /><link rel="canonical" href={canonical} /><link rel="icon" href="/field-index/assets/field-index-mark.svg" type="image/svg+xml" /><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" /><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin /><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Newsreader:opsz,wght@6..72,500;6..72,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" /><link rel="stylesheet" href="/field-index/assets/field-index.css" /><title>Editorial Policy — Coreweaver Field Index</title></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#policy">Skip to policy</a><header class="masthead"><a class="wordmark" href="/field-index"><img src="/field-index/assets/field-index-mark.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" /><span><strong>COREWEAVER</strong><small>FIELD INDEX / 001</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Field Index navigation"><a href="/field-index">Index</a><a href="/field-index/methodology">Methodology</a><a href="/">Coreweaver Labs ↗</a></nav></header><main class="content-main" id="policy"><div class="section-kicker"><span>03</span> Editorial policy</div><h1>Independence needs a <em>visible process.</em></h1><p class="content-lede">The Field Index makes source boundaries, caveats, and correction routes visible because an infrastructure reference should be open to challenge. Editorial selection is not a substitute for reader judgment or primary-source review.</p><section class="content-block"><h2>Selection and source standard</h2><p>Records are selected for their documented relevance to agentic AI infrastructure, governance, security, interoperability, or public-interest stewardship. A named primary public source is required. Secondary analysis may help identify candidates, but it should not carry a core factual claim when a direct public source is available.</p></section><section class="content-block"><h2>No paid placement or rankings</h2><p>The Index does not sell inclusion, better placement, ratings, or favorable summaries. Listing order is an interface convention, not a performance hierarchy. A source link can explain a record’s documented scope; it cannot prove quality, safety, security, adoption, or approval beyond what the source states.</p></section><section class="content-block"><h2>AI assistance disclosure</h2><p>Automation may assist with retrieval, metadata consistency, duplicate detection, or drafting a review proposal. A human editor must review source-linked factual claims before publication and remains responsible for corrections. AI-generated text is not treated as a source.</p></section><section class="content-block"><h2>Corrections and challenges</h2><p>To challenge a record, email <a href="mailto:hello@coreweaverlabs.com?subject=Field%20Index%20correction">hello@coreweaverlabs.com</a> with the record ID, proposed correction, and a public supporting source. Material changes should result in a dated change-log note, a narrowed claim, or removal. The original source should be revisited before a correction is published.</p></section><section class="content-block"><h2>Conflicts and relationships</h2><p>Where Coreweaver Labs has a material relationship with a record or source, it should be disclosed in the record. In the absence of such a disclosure, readers must not infer independence, affiliation, approval, or shared governance from inclusion alone.</p><a class="text-link" href="/field-index/methodology">Read methodology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section></main><footer><div class="footer__brand"><img src="/field-index/assets/field-index-mark.svg" alt="" width="36" height="36" /><span>COREWEAVER FIELD INDEX / 001</span></div><p>Source-led infrastructure records for an accountable agentic AI field.</p><a href="/field-index">Return to Index ↗</a></footer></body></html>
